    model: "Sunil, 42, presents with a third depressive episode and residual symptoms between episodes. A family history of recurrent depression and a long ruminative style (predisposing) raise his risk; a stressful new role with evening calls (precipitating) set off this episode. Stopping medicine soon after feeling better, untreated residual symptoms and rumination (perpetuating) explain why it keeps returning. Each new episode raises the risk of the next, which is why the aim now is full remission and long-term maintenance. In CBT terms the rumination is the key target, and mindfulness-based cognitive therapy is designed to prevent relapse in recurrent depression. His wife's watchfulness and his interest in mindfulness (protective) fit a written relapse prevention plan. His employer and his coffee are distractors.",
